From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:55:00 +0800
Subject: spi: qcom-geni: wait for the transfer queue to stop before shutdown

The SPI core times out waiting for a busy queue. On GENI, error
recovery can still be waiting for GPI termination at that point.
Keep waiting rather than return from shutdown while DMA may still
be active. The queued worker retains the transfer, mappings and
runtime-PM reference while it confirms termination.

Fixes: 3958b39fa5b7 ("spi: qcom-geni: Add shutdown callback to quiesce hardware on reboot")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
index 1d56bccbe6fdf91dd06c6da877c86c4b91ed5c94..1e6202cf5edf37e36de47b257a3e76871845fd32 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -1140,7 +1140,10 @@ static void spi_geni_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct spi_controller *spi = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	spi_controller_suspend(spi);
+	/* Keep resources until queued transfers have stopped. */
+	while (spi_controller_suspend(spi))
+		dev_err_ratelimited(&pdev->dev,
+				    "SPI queue still busy; waiting before shutdown\n");
 }
 
 static int spi_geni_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
